From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:09:04 +0900
Subject: Android host: the desktop session survives the host going away

When the Android host (the Rungic app) was closed, killed (a vendor's battery manager, low memory),
updated or restarted, KWin exited with 133 for kwin_wayland_wrapper to restart it, and the app then
restarted the whole desktop session: every window and anything unsaved was lost, though the Linux
container and its processes were alive.

Now the lost connection is reported once and never read again (WaylandDisplay). The phone's output
stays for the workspace and its clients: with no output at all plasmashell exits (its panels get a
zero-width layer surface on the placeholder screen, a protocol error). The output stops rendering,
drops the frames still waiting for the host and the buffers leased from it, and destroys its host
window and the layers' subsurfaces (WaylandOutput::unbindHost). Cast outputs go with the host, as
do the input devices and the buffers imported on the connection (WaylandBackend::disconnectHost).
The dead display stays allocated, as proxies of it may still be released. Every 500 ms the backend
checks whether the host's socket answers, then connects again (connectHost, without the initial
60 s wait): the output gets a new host window and subsurfaces, is configured by the host (a size
the host changed meanwhile is taken as any host resize) and draws its next frame in full; a new
seat, the host's globals, text input and idle inhibition follow.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-05
X-Rungic-Status: Pending
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:session.ready
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/72
Origin: vendor
